d 'EASI': module to estimate the Exact Affine Stone Index demand system
d
d  easi estimates the Exact Affine Stone Index (EASI) implicit
d Marshallian demand system of Lewbel and Pendakur (2009) within
d Stata and Mata, by iterated linear three-stage least squares with
d Slutsky symmetry imposed. It reports expenditure, compensated and
d uncompensated price, and demographic elasticities for the
d households, the individuals, or the market, with standard errors
d from the influence functions of the whole procedure; sampling
d weights, robust, cluster and survey-design (svyset) variance, and
d a design bootstrap. The households that do not buy some goods are
d handled by imputing their missing prices (pimpute) and by the
d Shonkwiler-Yen correction for censoring (selection), both carried
d into the standard errors. easidiag diagnoses the data before
d estimation; predict and estat engel give the Engel curves; tables
d with significance stars can be written to Word, LaTeX, Excel, CSV
d or Markdown; a dialog box and help examples run from clickable
d links are included. sr_easi is kept as a backward-compatible
d wrapper. A technical note documents the model, the estimator and
d the validation of the standard errors; it is included as an
d ancillary file (easi_technical_note.pdf) 
d
d KW: demand system
d KW: EASI
d KW: Exact Affine Stone Index
d KW: price elasticities
d KW: household survey
d KW: censoring
d KW: survey design
d KW: three-stage least squares
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.2
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260930
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar,  Universite Laval 
d Support: email aabd@@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
